WEBVTT

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:25.483
<i>Twenty meters to the target point.</i>

00:00:26.109 --> 00:00:28.570
<i>Earthquakes have made the area unstable.</i>

00:00:28.653 --> 00:00:30.989
<i>Come back up the moment you sense</i>
<i>any disturbance.</i>

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:37.495
This stratum is made up of flood sediment?

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:48.715
There's no mistaking it. This is it.

00:00:56.097 --> 00:00:57.223
Huh?

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:00.560
Incredible.

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:03.730
A cavern like this inside the mountain.

00:01:05.607 --> 00:01:07.275
Hey, what's that?

00:01:13.031 --> 00:01:16.242
Holy crap, it's really here.

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:27.378
<i>Here, there is a single plate.</i>

00:01:28.338 --> 00:01:31.800
<i>The message it carries</i>
<i>is a warning to us in the present.</i>

00:01:31.883 --> 00:01:34.719
<i>From an advanced ancient civilization</i>

00:01:34.803 --> 00:01:36.888
<i>that grew too advanced</i>

00:01:36.971 --> 00:01:38.556
<i>and was destroyed.</i>

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:41.476
<i>This is their message.</i>

00:01:41.559 --> 00:01:44.604
<i>"Protect our heritage from the wicked."</i>

00:01:45.897 --> 00:01:49.150
<i>Trusting in this message,</i>
<i>one organization strives</i>

00:01:49.234 --> 00:01:52.987
<i>to keep the advanced</i>
<i>ancient civilization sealed away.</i>

00:01:53.071 --> 00:01:56.407
<i>The special operatives</i>
<i>of that organization are called</i>

00:01:57.534 --> 00:01:59.285
<i>"Spriggan."</i>

00:03:02.599 --> 00:03:03.766
Ominae!

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:06.019
Wake up, Ominae!

00:03:09.981 --> 00:03:11.566
I said, wake up!

00:03:17.947 --> 00:03:21.284
Ominae!

00:03:23.453 --> 00:03:25.872
Hey, "Eternal Truant,"

00:03:25.955 --> 00:03:28.166
I can't believe you finally
came back to school

00:03:28.249 --> 00:03:29.918
just to sleep your way through class.

00:03:30.001 --> 00:03:32.503
People are being really mean
to our class president, Kagaho,

00:03:32.587 --> 00:03:34.047
all because of you, you know.

00:03:34.130 --> 00:03:35.757
Oh, Hatsuho…

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:38.676
It is what it is. I was up all night with…

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:40.762
All night with what?

00:03:40.845 --> 00:03:43.473
A game! I stayed up all night
playing a video game, okay?

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:45.016
Oh, really? Were you?

00:03:45.099 --> 00:03:46.768
You weren't having
a different kind of fun?

00:03:46.851 --> 00:03:49.687
-Shut up!
-Anyway…

00:03:49.771 --> 00:03:52.148
you're going to fix
your poor lifestyle habits,

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:54.901
and your slacker tendencies
starting today.

00:03:54.984 --> 00:03:56.903
Isn't that right, Class President Kagaho?

00:03:56.986 --> 00:03:57.862
Huh?

00:03:57.946 --> 00:04:01.115
Uh, well, I… um…

00:04:01.824 --> 00:04:03.618
I mean…

00:04:03.701 --> 00:04:07.163
Um, see you tomorrow, if that's okay.

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:08.957
Kagaho.

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:10.708
Are you guys actually twins?

00:04:10.792 --> 00:04:12.335
Just shut up!

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:13.628
All right.

00:04:13.711 --> 00:04:15.546
So I'll come to class tomorrow as well.

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:16.881
Oh, really?

00:04:16.965 --> 00:04:18.633
Yeah, I'll take care of it.

00:04:18.716 --> 00:04:21.886
Uh, you do know that's how attendance
works anyway, don't you?

00:04:21.970 --> 00:04:23.763
Huh?

00:04:25.848 --> 00:04:28.142
Sorry, looks like tomorrow's a no-go.

00:04:28.226 --> 00:04:31.145
What? But you just told us
that you'd come to class.

00:04:31.229 --> 00:04:33.523
Don't even think about skipping
after-school practice.

00:04:33.606 --> 00:04:34.857
Sorry, but something came up.

00:04:34.941 --> 00:04:38.152
Let's take a rain check.

00:04:38.945 --> 00:04:40.697
-You think this is a joke?
-Huh?

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:43.825
If you wanna leave, then first,
you have to go through me!

00:04:43.908 --> 00:04:47.370
Hey now, I thought karate club members
weren't supposed to use violence?

00:04:47.453 --> 00:04:50.707
Quit whining and give up already!

00:04:51.624 --> 00:04:52.583
Oh.

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:55.795
Wait! No way!

00:04:55.878 --> 00:04:57.880
Ominae?

00:05:00.049 --> 00:05:01.426
See ya!

00:05:07.056 --> 00:05:10.143
Oh, well.
He's getting held back a year for sure.

00:05:14.564 --> 00:05:17.108
It's Noah's Ark? From the bible?

00:05:17.191 --> 00:05:18.568
<i>That's the one.</i>

00:05:18.651 --> 00:05:21.863
<i>For a while, ARCAM has been doing</i>
<i>a long-term survey of Mount Ararat,</i>

00:05:21.946 --> 00:05:23.906
<i>with permission from</i>
<i>the Turkish Government.</i>

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:27.201
<i>But then, three years ago,</i>
<i>observation of muon particles</i>

00:05:27.285 --> 00:05:30.204
<i>led to the discovery</i>
<i>of an unnatural cave formation.</i>

00:05:30.288 --> 00:05:32.832
<i>When the survey team went inside</i>
<i>the cave to investigate,</i>

00:05:32.915 --> 00:05:35.960
<i>they discovered the hull of a ship</i>
<i>buried right there on the bedrock.</i>

00:05:36.044 --> 00:05:37.754
<i>Well, that's insanely lucky.</i>

00:05:37.837 --> 00:05:40.673
<i>So why is it this is the first time</i>
<i>I'm hearing about this find.</i>

00:05:40.757 --> 00:05:44.218
Everything to do with the Ark
is top secret information.

00:05:44.302 --> 00:05:47.972
Besides, you weren't even with
the ARCAM organization three years ago.

00:05:48.056 --> 00:05:49.891
<i>Oh, come on,</i>
<i>when this gets announced,</i>

00:05:49.974 --> 00:05:53.478
<i>it'll be an even bigger shake-up</i>
<i>for academia than the ruins of Troy.</i>

00:05:53.561 --> 00:05:55.938
As things stand now,
we can't let that happen.

00:05:56.022 --> 00:05:57.398
All thanks to…

00:05:57.482 --> 00:05:59.734
-<i>…this thing here.</i>
-<i>Hm?</i>

00:05:59.817 --> 00:06:01.402
A new Message Plate?

00:06:01.486 --> 00:06:04.405
<i>Exactly, we found this one two weeks ago.</i>

00:06:04.489 --> 00:06:06.991
<i>It was embedded</i>
<i>in the outer cladding of the ship.</i>

00:06:07.784 --> 00:06:11.120
<i>This plate is made from the same material</i>
<i>as the ones we found before.</i>

00:06:11.746 --> 00:06:14.207
<i>The issue we had is with the message.</i>

00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:17.752
<i>According to our translators,</i>
<i>the ancient Hebrew says,</i>

00:06:18.336 --> 00:06:21.631
<i>"Noah bestows grace</i>
<i>upon all living things."</i>

00:06:21.714 --> 00:06:25.176
<i>"Noah brings destruction</i>
<i>to all living things."</i>

00:06:26.594 --> 00:06:27.804
<i>What does that mean?</i>

00:06:27.887 --> 00:06:31.391
I don't know, however,
we can infer that Noah's Ark

00:06:31.474 --> 00:06:34.936
possesses two opposing powers,
both grace and destruction.

00:06:35.019 --> 00:06:38.106
And therefore, it could be dangerous
depending on how it's used.

00:06:38.731 --> 00:06:41.484
As expected, we've had several reports

00:06:41.567 --> 00:06:44.028
that the Ark's survey team
along with their base camp

00:06:44.112 --> 00:06:47.156
located nearby have been under attack
for the past several days.

00:06:48.199 --> 00:06:50.701
<i>They're holding off</i>
<i>the attackers by the skin of their teeth.</i>

00:06:50.785 --> 00:06:52.745
<i>But we don't know</i>
<i>where the attack came from.</i>

00:06:52.829 --> 00:06:55.081
<i>And neither Turkey</i>
<i>nor any of the surrounding countries</i>

00:06:55.164 --> 00:06:56.749
<i>have released a statement.</i>

00:06:56.833 --> 00:06:59.794
<i>We aren't in a position</i>
<i>to make the same public, either.</i>

00:07:01.504 --> 00:07:07.260
Yu, your primary objective is to help
protect the members of that survey team.

00:07:07.343 --> 00:07:10.221
And also, if our suspicions are correct,

00:07:10.304 --> 00:07:13.141
that Noah's Ark really is
a dangerous ancient relic,

00:07:13.224 --> 00:07:16.727
seal it away.
And if you can't, then destroy it.

00:07:17.395 --> 00:07:21.315
NOAH'S ARK

00:07:22.358 --> 00:07:24.694
Yu Ominae, isn't it, sir?

00:07:25.528 --> 00:07:27.822
<i>We have intel that an ARCAM-owned plane</i>

00:07:27.905 --> 00:07:30.366
<i>took off from Haneda airport</i>
<i>two hours ago.</i>

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:33.411
<i>It is likely that the agent on board…</i>

00:07:33.494 --> 00:07:34.829
<i>is this boy.</i>

00:07:34.912 --> 00:07:38.332
This kid's a Spriggan. S-rank Special Op.

00:07:38.416 --> 00:07:40.293
This is gonna mean trouble for us.

00:07:40.376 --> 00:07:41.586
What do you think we should do?

00:07:41.669 --> 00:07:44.714
At this rate, I'm afraid we're gonna risk
ARCAM sealing away the Ark.

00:07:44.797 --> 00:07:46.591
There's no cause for concern…

00:07:47.341 --> 00:07:48.634
'cause this is my job.

00:07:48.718 --> 00:07:51.888
And it's the entire reason
we were sent here to begin with.

00:07:51.971 --> 00:07:54.348
We're here to take commands
since you proved unable

00:07:54.432 --> 00:07:56.601
to handle a few civilians playing soldier.

00:07:58.686 --> 00:08:00.563
<i>Colonel MacDougall, sir.</i>

00:08:00.646 --> 00:08:04.025
<i>We've been dealing with the government</i>
<i>in Turkey and Armenia,</i>

00:08:04.108 --> 00:08:07.111
<i>but any further action</i>
<i>could harm diplomatic relations.</i>

00:08:07.195 --> 00:08:09.989
<i>You are the final reinforcements.</i>

00:08:10.072 --> 00:08:11.866
This is plenty.

00:08:11.949 --> 00:08:15.369
They can send as many Spriggans
as they please.

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:19.832
<i>I'll turn this mountain into their grave.</i>

00:08:21.334 --> 00:08:23.211
We've been waiting for you, kiddo.

00:08:23.294 --> 00:08:25.880
Man, it sure is a relief
having you here, Yu.

00:08:25.963 --> 00:08:27.798
Hey there, Bruce! Hiya, Ed!

00:08:27.882 --> 00:08:29.383
Sounds like you guys have had a rough…

00:08:29.467 --> 00:08:31.511
Come on, whatever. This is nothing.

00:08:31.594 --> 00:08:33.971
Kevin, hey! Congrats on the wedding, man!

00:08:34.055 --> 00:08:37.975
Once this mission wraps up, she and I
are honeymooning on the southern islands.

00:08:38.059 --> 00:08:41.479
That's all on hold until the Ark
opens up its doors though.

00:08:41.562 --> 00:08:44.190
It's just you and your imagination.

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:48.694
-Yu!
-Huh?

00:08:55.409 --> 00:08:57.954
Your Orichalcum fighting knife.

00:08:58.037 --> 00:09:01.791
And it's crafted with a knuckle guard
just as you requested.

00:09:01.874 --> 00:09:03.584
This is great.

00:09:03.668 --> 00:09:05.545
Orichalcum is a wonder.

00:09:05.628 --> 00:09:09.423
It's essentially a metal that hardens
as pressures are applied to it.

00:09:09.507 --> 00:09:13.886
And, until now, the hardest
was just over 10 on the Mohs scale,

00:09:13.970 --> 00:09:16.389
about three times as hard as a diamond.

00:09:16.472 --> 00:09:19.392
This knife, however,
was refined specifically

00:09:19.475 --> 00:09:21.936
to increase the hardness of the blade.

00:09:22.019 --> 00:09:24.647
Its strength far exceeds anything
up until now.

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:26.691
This is great, Professor Meyzel.

00:09:26.774 --> 00:09:29.443
I knew I could count on you
to make this bad boy.

00:09:29.527 --> 00:09:32.280
There is something else
I brought along for you.

00:09:32.363 --> 00:09:33.739
Ready, Margaret?

00:09:33.823 --> 00:09:35.199
Yes, Professor.

00:09:37.535 --> 00:09:40.496
These arm pads
are fitted with anchor wire.

00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:43.082
Inside is an ultra-high performance motor

00:09:43.165 --> 00:09:46.294
capable of lifting the equivalent
of two to three people.

00:09:46.877 --> 00:09:48.963
Wow. These are gonna be fun.

00:09:49.046 --> 00:09:53.092
<i>Warning, armed forces</i>
<i>have been detected near the facility.</i>

00:09:53.175 --> 00:09:54.760
<i>Affiliation unknown!</i>

00:09:54.844 --> 00:09:58.723
<i>Medical teams are to accompany</i>
<i>each squad to the site ASAP.</i>

00:09:58.806 --> 00:10:01.017
Guess that means
we're done catching up, huh?

00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:03.769
Right. I'm gonna take these for a spin.

00:10:03.853 --> 00:10:05.021
Go ahead.

00:10:05.104 --> 00:10:08.649
Oh, a friend of yours
is supposed to be here soon, too.

00:10:08.733 --> 00:10:10.651
Uh, what was their name again?

00:10:10.735 --> 00:10:11.569
You know…

00:10:11.652 --> 00:10:14.905
the, uh… the French one with long hair.

00:10:17.742 --> 00:10:19.994
Don't let them get near
the line of defense.

00:10:20.077 --> 00:10:21.412
Concentrate fire!

00:10:23.748 --> 00:10:25.791
It keeps dodging everything!

00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:35.343
Is that the Machiner's Platoon?

00:10:36.010 --> 00:10:38.679
So it's the United States
who's trying to steal the Ark?

00:11:03.412 --> 00:11:04.789
Touchdown!

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:09.335
What is that thing?

00:11:09.418 --> 00:11:10.503
Retreat!

00:11:10.586 --> 00:11:13.005
All troops fall back
to the second line of defense!

00:11:18.761 --> 00:11:21.931
All you have to do
was kindly leave Noah to us.

00:11:22.014 --> 00:11:23.933
No one would've died.

00:11:24.016 --> 00:11:25.935
Here's a juicy question for you.

00:11:26.018 --> 00:11:28.896
I'd like to know
whether you prefer mince or ham?

00:11:39.073 --> 00:11:41.158
I guess, you're a ham fan, then.

00:11:44.412 --> 00:11:45.913
Hey, Little Boy.

00:11:45.996 --> 00:11:49.041
ARCAM is too damn weak. I'm bored.

00:11:49.125 --> 00:11:51.085
Well, that's not my fault, Fatman.

00:11:51.168 --> 00:11:54.547
I mean, did they really think they could
take out our assassination squad

00:11:54.630 --> 00:11:55.756
with this garbage?

00:11:55.840 --> 00:11:57.925
ARCAM is so naïve.

00:12:00.261 --> 00:12:01.679
Who the hell are you?

00:12:02.263 --> 00:12:03.514
It's the Spriggan.

00:12:03.597 --> 00:12:04.598
He's here.

00:12:05.182 --> 00:12:06.851
Yu Ominae!

00:12:08.853 --> 00:12:10.688
Yu! Yu.

00:12:10.771 --> 00:12:15.609
SOFIA, ABOUT WHEN DO YOU THINK
YOU'LL COME BACK?

00:12:16.193 --> 00:12:17.111
You bastards.

00:12:17.903 --> 00:12:20.740
You're telling me,
you really want the Ark this badly?

00:12:20.823 --> 00:12:23.117
Want it?

00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:25.286
"Want" has nothing to do with it.

00:12:25.369 --> 00:12:27.955
A relic with incredible power
like Noah's Ark

00:12:28.038 --> 00:12:30.207
should be under America's control.

00:12:30.291 --> 00:12:32.376
Yeah. We're just delivering justice,

00:12:32.460 --> 00:12:34.795
making things how they're supposed to be.

00:12:38.007 --> 00:12:39.258
Justice?

00:12:41.177 --> 00:12:43.304
You bastards think this is funny?

00:12:44.263 --> 00:12:47.183
You're not getting out of these mountains
in one piece.

00:12:47.266 --> 00:12:49.143
Armor up!

00:12:50.144 --> 00:12:52.146
Try me!

00:12:52.229 --> 00:12:54.774
We aren't weaklings like Hummingbat.

00:12:58.110 --> 00:13:01.697
Try all you want, but you won't
take me down like that.

00:13:15.878 --> 00:13:17.254
Do you like that, Spriggan?

00:13:17.838 --> 00:13:19.089
Run! Run!

00:13:19.173 --> 00:13:22.510
A single fragment hits your head
and it's game over.

00:13:23.385 --> 00:13:24.303
Huh?

00:13:35.648 --> 00:13:36.690
Little Boy!

00:13:37.274 --> 00:13:38.692
You runt!

00:13:41.737 --> 00:13:43.781
You think I'm playing around?

00:13:44.990 --> 00:13:46.534
Too slow!

00:13:48.077 --> 00:13:48.994
Damn brat!

00:13:57.378 --> 00:14:00.256
The texture…

00:14:06.136 --> 00:14:08.430
I got you now, Spriggan!

00:14:09.181 --> 00:14:12.184
You… your body armor…

00:14:12.268 --> 00:14:16.647
That's right, they're made
of Orichalcum just like yours!

00:14:16.730 --> 00:14:19.024
You thought ARCAM had a monopoly

00:14:19.108 --> 00:14:21.861
on repurposing OOPArts as weapons?

00:14:21.944 --> 00:14:25.155
Now that our body armor specs match yours,

00:14:25.239 --> 00:14:27.283
we're undefeatable.

00:14:29.034 --> 00:14:30.619
Do it, Fatman!

00:14:30.703 --> 00:14:32.538
Snap his little neck already!

00:14:32.621 --> 00:14:34.790
I hear you, Little Boy!

00:14:48.387 --> 00:14:50.431
Hey, Ominae.

00:14:50.514 --> 00:14:53.684
A second-rate performance, as usual.

00:14:53.767 --> 00:14:56.812
That's now 10 times you'd be dead
without me.

00:14:56.896 --> 00:14:59.356
Wh-Who the hell are you?

00:14:59.440 --> 00:15:01.817
Didn't your mother
teach you to use your manners

00:15:01.901 --> 00:15:03.402
when you ask someone's name?

00:15:04.737 --> 00:15:07.406
My name is Jacquemonde to you.

00:15:07.489 --> 00:15:10.910
Spriggan, Jean Jacquemonde to be precise.

00:15:10.993 --> 00:15:13.120
That guy's a Spriggan?

00:15:13.203 --> 00:15:15.164
Another one?

00:15:15.247 --> 00:15:17.708
Lose the cool guy act, asshole!

00:15:17.791 --> 00:15:20.669
You sure talk big after showing up late.

00:15:20.753 --> 00:15:25.174
Well, if I'd been here from the beginning
then you wouldn't have gotten a turn.

00:15:25.257 --> 00:15:28.969
And what are you doing letting this scum
get the better of you anyway, huh?

00:15:29.053 --> 00:15:30.554
Shut the hell up!

00:15:33.140 --> 00:15:34.224
Jean!

00:15:36.185 --> 00:15:38.938
The one you have to worry about is me!

00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:44.109
Yeah, that's what happens
when you mess with the two of us.

00:15:44.193 --> 00:15:45.361
You got that?

00:15:46.195 --> 00:15:47.863
Hey halfwit, I'm over here.

00:15:47.947 --> 00:15:49.198
-Try to keep up.
-Huh?

00:15:51.241 --> 00:15:52.534
I made a vow

00:15:52.618 --> 00:15:56.038
that I, Jean Jacquemonde, would rid
the world of all the bottom feeders

00:15:56.121 --> 00:15:57.706
just like you.

00:15:59.583 --> 00:16:00.834
Shut up!

00:16:08.133 --> 00:16:10.678
How's he so damn fast?

00:16:17.434 --> 00:16:21.146
Ah, Orichalcum body armor, huh?

00:16:21.230 --> 00:16:23.732
Guess, there's only one option left.

00:16:23.816 --> 00:16:26.944
I'll just hit that ugly mug
sticking out the top.

00:16:29.071 --> 00:16:31.156
Running away, Spriggan?

00:16:32.574 --> 00:16:33.492
Here, catch!

00:16:43.043 --> 00:16:44.545
Damn runt!

00:16:56.724 --> 00:17:01.145
Damn it! Damn it!
Damn it! Damn it!

00:17:01.228 --> 00:17:05.149
I'm the fastest one
in the Machiner's Platoon by a mile.

00:17:05.232 --> 00:17:07.276
How the hell is he keeping up with me?

00:17:13.782 --> 00:17:17.327
You… you… you demon!

00:17:20.289 --> 00:17:22.708
The only demon I see here is you.

00:17:34.178 --> 00:17:36.096
Was that all you've got?

00:17:40.517 --> 00:17:45.564
See, it hurts my feelings getting called
a demon by a freak show like you.

00:17:47.691 --> 00:17:49.109
Stay away!

00:17:49.193 --> 00:17:50.944
You demon!

00:17:51.570 --> 00:17:53.989
Not the brightest, are you?

00:17:56.533 --> 00:18:00.079
I'll fix that disgusting mug
of yours for you.

00:18:00.704 --> 00:18:02.081
Are you ready?

00:18:12.299 --> 00:18:13.759
Little Boy!

00:18:23.352 --> 00:18:24.436
Damn you!

00:18:32.569 --> 00:18:33.904
Impossible!

00:18:33.987 --> 00:18:36.782
My Orichalcum body armor!

00:18:37.491 --> 00:18:38.909
Aw, you're so naïve.

00:18:38.992 --> 00:18:42.704
You thought that outfit you're so pleased
with wouldn't go out of style?

00:18:43.372 --> 00:18:45.707
And now, I'm gonna make you suffer…

00:18:45.791 --> 00:18:49.294
nice and slow for each one of my friends
that you killed.

00:18:49.878 --> 00:18:53.841
You… you scum! I swear!

00:18:53.924 --> 00:18:57.553
I'm gonna slaughter every last one of you!

00:19:05.144 --> 00:19:08.480
You murdered my friends
like they were nothing.

00:19:09.565 --> 00:19:11.191
Feel their pain!

00:19:27.541 --> 00:19:30.586
My limbs! What have you done to my limbs?
You bastard!

00:19:32.171 --> 00:19:34.631
So sorry, I didn't see you down there.

00:19:34.715 --> 00:19:37.676
Can you show me where it hurts?
Maybe I can help you out.

00:19:37.759 --> 00:19:39.428
Where should I start?

00:19:39.511 --> 00:19:41.972
Your head? Your heart?

00:19:42.055 --> 00:19:45.934
Don't get cocky, runt.

00:19:46.018 --> 00:19:48.312
After killing us,

00:19:48.395 --> 00:19:52.191
there's no way you're leaving
this mountain alive.

00:19:52.274 --> 00:19:55.694
Hey, Ominae.
This one's still alive.

00:19:55.777 --> 00:19:58.030
Yeah, I made sure
not to hit anything vital.

00:19:58.113 --> 00:19:59.156
Huh?

00:19:59.239 --> 00:20:01.033
I got a mountain
of questions for him.

00:20:03.202 --> 00:20:07.748
The Ark will belong to America.

00:20:07.831 --> 00:20:12.336
We'll have it and in the meantime,
you're just keeping it safe for us.

00:20:13.503 --> 00:20:17.007
Against the power that we have,
ARCAM doesn't stand--

00:20:23.013 --> 00:20:24.848
All right, it's your turn now.

00:20:26.058 --> 00:20:27.476
That's enough, you idiot!

00:20:27.559 --> 00:20:28.894
There's no fight left in him.

00:20:28.977 --> 00:20:31.063
Who are you calling an idiot, idiot?

00:20:31.146 --> 00:20:34.316
Do you know how many of our allies
these two assholes just killed?

00:20:34.399 --> 00:20:37.319
Are you thinking of showing mercy
to the enemy, huh?

00:20:37.402 --> 00:20:38.820
No, I'm not thinking that at all.

00:20:38.904 --> 00:20:41.198
But we're not murderers.
We're better than them.

00:20:41.281 --> 00:20:42.658
And if--

00:20:42.741 --> 00:20:46.245
Honestly, Ominae,
you're so soft, it makes me sick.

00:20:46.745 --> 00:20:49.206
Listen up, when you are a Spriggan,

00:20:49.289 --> 00:20:52.459
you guard ARCAM,
as well as all the artifacts.

00:20:52.542 --> 00:20:56.922
And to guard it, we have to be the most
powerful as well as the most feared.

00:20:57.798 --> 00:21:01.551
If you let them off lightly now,
you'll regret it later.

00:21:06.348 --> 00:21:08.642
Confirmed, Fatman's vital signs
have ceased.

00:21:09.393 --> 00:21:11.645
Little Boy isn't answering his coms.

00:21:11.728 --> 00:21:13.647
We can assume he's been taken prisoner.

00:21:13.730 --> 00:21:16.316
That was within the scope
of my predictions.

00:21:16.400 --> 00:21:20.362
Their task was to destabilize ARCAM
and weaken their military capabilities.

00:21:20.445 --> 00:21:23.657
And they carried it out most admirably.

00:21:23.740 --> 00:21:27.744
But what's gonna happen if ARCAM
does manage to take the Ark anyway?

00:21:27.828 --> 00:21:31.456
Even if ARCAM has the key,
they certainly won't have ascertained

00:21:31.540 --> 00:21:33.083
how to use it.

00:21:33.166 --> 00:21:36.545
You see, only with my power…

00:21:36.628 --> 00:21:40.841
and the ancient writings of Noah
can one enter the Ark.

00:21:40.924 --> 00:21:43.552
It would be impossible for them
to get there before us.

00:21:43.635 --> 00:21:46.305
Hm. Colonel MacDougall, sir.

00:21:46.388 --> 00:21:50.559
Wouldn't you say this situation
merits requesting backup?

00:21:54.396 --> 00:21:58.317
The Pentagon has bestowed
upon me the power of God.

00:21:58.900 --> 00:22:01.111
Not only that, but now with Noah,

00:22:01.194 --> 00:22:04.323
I have been given the chance
to commune with the true God.

00:22:07.409 --> 00:22:10.620
I will kill anyone
who dares get in my way.

00:22:12.039 --> 00:22:16.209
All you need to do is listen to me
and do whatever it is I tell you.

00:22:21.048 --> 00:22:22.257
We're here.

00:22:22.341 --> 00:22:24.343
That is Noah's Ark.

00:22:27.054 --> 00:22:28.764
It's massive.

00:22:28.847 --> 00:22:32.559
What you see here
is something akin to the rudder, or keel.

00:22:32.642 --> 00:22:34.936
The whole of the ship
is up above the bedrock.

00:22:35.479 --> 00:22:38.148
They must be after
whatever's in the Ark, right?

00:22:38.231 --> 00:22:40.817
Then why don't we just
drill a hole in it already?

00:22:40.901 --> 00:22:42.486
-Focus, young man.
-Huh?

00:22:42.569 --> 00:22:45.405
A hole?
We can't even leave a scratch on it.

00:22:45.489 --> 00:22:46.698
Why is that?

00:22:47.991 --> 00:22:49.785
Because of the way it was made.

00:22:49.868 --> 00:22:54.498
The Ark is made from the same
frozen entire material as this plate.

00:22:55.082 --> 00:22:57.376
Time does not move for it.

00:22:57.459 --> 00:23:00.962
It cannot change, and thus,
it cannot be destroyed.

00:23:01.046 --> 00:23:03.382
So why are you
investigating the plates?

00:23:03.465 --> 00:23:05.425
Shouldn't the Ark be higher priority?

00:23:05.509 --> 00:23:10.305
The mechanism of this plate is different
from other ones we've seen.

00:23:10.389 --> 00:23:12.849
When we apply a small electric current,

00:23:12.933 --> 00:23:15.644
it generates a bizarre magnetic field.

00:23:15.727 --> 00:23:20.357
That current is the exact same voltage as
the one that is flowing through the Ark.

00:23:20.440 --> 00:23:23.860
I, therefore, believe
it must be some kind of key.

00:23:23.944 --> 00:23:27.072
Well, if you've worked out that much,
just open it.

00:23:27.155 --> 00:23:28.573
Foolish again.

00:23:28.657 --> 00:23:30.867
It appears that we are still missing

00:23:30.951 --> 00:23:33.203
one of the pieces needed to awaken Noah.

00:23:33.954 --> 00:23:36.123
Something other than the key.

00:23:37.290 --> 00:23:39.876
Heat source detected at point Delta 1-4.

00:23:40.627 --> 00:23:42.337
The source is slow but moving.

00:23:43.922 --> 00:23:45.632
Is that a kid?

00:23:49.886 --> 00:23:51.638
-Jean!
-We should split up.

00:23:54.015 --> 00:23:55.851
What are you laughing at?

00:23:57.018 --> 00:24:00.480
He's here.
The child with the power of the Devil.

00:24:01.606 --> 00:24:06.862
You and the Spriggans are all going
to die here in this mountain.

00:24:07.737 --> 00:24:09.906
It's no use! Guns have no effect!

00:24:09.990 --> 00:24:11.324
Close the bulkheads!

00:24:11.408 --> 00:24:13.577
Don't let them advance any further!

00:24:31.553 --> 00:24:35.432
My team and I have this area
totally under our control.

00:24:35.515 --> 00:24:39.436
Lay down your little weapons and hand
over that Message Plate key right now.

00:24:40.020 --> 00:24:41.605
Who the hell are you?

00:24:41.688 --> 00:24:42.606
Huh?

00:24:42.689 --> 00:24:45.233
I don't know what you want with the Ark,

00:24:45.317 --> 00:24:48.236
but I've got no interest
in giving it to you.

00:24:49.362 --> 00:24:50.989
Oh, all right.

00:24:51.740 --> 00:24:54.409
I suppose there's nothing else
I can do then.

00:24:57.496 --> 00:25:00.373
You… you little…

00:25:01.374 --> 00:25:03.793
What have you done to me?

00:25:09.007 --> 00:25:10.008
Yu!

00:25:10.091 --> 00:25:12.844
Maybe you should refrain
from pointless resistance.

00:25:12.928 --> 00:25:15.514
Unless, of course,
you all want to die like him.

00:25:17.057 --> 00:25:18.725
-Hold on a second.
-Huh?

00:25:19.684 --> 00:25:21.686
Who's saying that I'm dead?

00:25:22.312 --> 00:25:23.730
How impressive.

00:25:23.813 --> 00:25:26.858
You must be tough to have survived
my psychokinesis.

00:25:26.942 --> 00:25:29.319
Almost like some kind of cockroach.

00:25:29.945 --> 00:25:33.323
You little twerp.
You calling me a cockroach?

00:25:33.406 --> 00:25:35.200
-Enough foolishness!
-Huh?

00:25:35.992 --> 00:25:37.786
I'll give you the key to the Ark.

00:25:37.869 --> 00:25:41.998
And in return, you will spare the lives
of everybody here.

00:25:42.082 --> 00:25:44.960
Ah, it's Professor Meyzel and Margaret!

00:25:45.544 --> 00:25:46.878
If you would be so kind…

00:25:46.962 --> 00:25:49.422
-as to accompany me as I enter the Ark.
-Stop, don't do it.

00:25:49.506 --> 00:25:51.007
Stop, Professor--

00:25:51.716 --> 00:25:53.426
I'll go with you, Colonel.

00:25:54.219 --> 00:25:56.179
My apologies, Margaret.

00:25:56.263 --> 00:25:58.807
I go wherever you go, Professor Meyzel.

00:25:58.890 --> 00:26:01.810
Touching. Then, come with me, won't you?

00:26:12.862 --> 00:26:15.782
You must be MacDougall from the Pentagon.

00:26:17.158 --> 00:26:20.954
I just can't imagine equipping a child
with such enhancements.

00:26:21.037 --> 00:26:24.749
My life is of no particular importance
outside of this mission.

00:26:24.833 --> 00:26:27.252
And besides, it's all thanks to this

00:26:27.335 --> 00:26:30.338
that I've been able
to get closer to God's power.

00:26:31.214 --> 00:26:32.674
God, huh?

00:26:33.341 --> 00:26:37.804
Seems more like the devil's handiwork
to me. An abomination.

00:26:42.183 --> 00:26:45.854
Time for you to join your friends
and their pointless death.

00:26:45.937 --> 00:26:46.980
Lieutenant,

00:26:47.063 --> 00:26:49.608
we were ordered to treat
the ARCAM soldiers as prisoners of war.

00:26:49.691 --> 00:26:50.900
No.

00:26:50.984 --> 00:26:53.028
I'm executing this one here.

00:26:53.111 --> 00:26:55.572
-But, sir--
-Quit your whining or you're next!

00:26:58.742 --> 00:27:03.538
What the hell? This entire place
has been overrun by the enemy?

00:27:03.622 --> 00:27:07.167
Oh, damn you, Jean Jacquemonde!

00:27:07.250 --> 00:27:10.629
None of you scum has any manners.

00:27:12.047 --> 00:27:13.882
No, you don't! Hiyah!

00:27:15.842 --> 00:27:18.386
You're pointing your little guns
at me? Really?

00:27:18.470 --> 00:27:20.972
You goons sure got some nerve!

00:27:28.521 --> 00:27:30.649
-Stop right there!
-Oh.

00:27:30.732 --> 00:27:33.526
Don't you care
about your little friend, huh?

00:27:33.610 --> 00:27:36.404
Ominae…

00:27:36.488 --> 00:27:38.740
Weren't you listening before?

00:27:38.823 --> 00:27:41.660
You'd have died 50 times already
without me.

00:27:46.414 --> 00:27:47.624
What?

00:27:51.836 --> 00:27:53.004
You fool!

00:27:53.088 --> 00:27:54.923
You're the dead one now!

00:27:57.008 --> 00:28:00.845
Well, you've done it now.
You filthy scumbag freaks.

00:28:01.513 --> 00:28:03.431
All right, it is what it is.

00:28:04.265 --> 00:28:07.936
Just you wait. You're gonna wish
you were already dead.

00:28:12.774 --> 00:28:15.151
Now then, little runt.

00:28:15.235 --> 00:28:17.779
Looks like it's finally your turn.

00:28:17.862 --> 00:28:20.156
I'll do you the favor
of sending you off

00:28:20.240 --> 00:28:21.866
with your little demon pal.

00:28:24.828 --> 00:28:26.579
Lieutenant…

00:28:26.663 --> 00:28:27.664
Lieutenant!

00:28:27.747 --> 00:28:28.873
Shut up!

00:28:33.294 --> 00:28:35.880
What the hell is that?

00:28:39.426 --> 00:28:41.970
Shoot it! Bring it down now!

00:28:49.728 --> 00:28:52.147
His… his wounds.
They're closing up!

00:28:52.230 --> 00:28:53.732
No way!

00:29:02.031 --> 00:29:03.867
Are you okay, Yu?

00:29:03.950 --> 00:29:05.618
Not me, the others.

00:29:05.702 --> 00:29:08.163
Like I'd leave you behind.

00:29:08.246 --> 00:29:10.623
But Jean… what's the matter with him?

00:29:11.166 --> 00:29:13.334
Jacquemonde is what's called
a lycanthrope.

00:29:13.418 --> 00:29:14.419
What?

00:29:14.502 --> 00:29:18.673
When he sees his own blood,
he turns into a beast.

00:29:20.258 --> 00:29:22.802
Once he changes, there's no stopping him.

00:29:22.886 --> 00:29:25.555
He'll keep going until he's slaughtered
everything that moves.

00:29:34.773 --> 00:29:36.399
This is Noah's Ark.

00:29:39.068 --> 00:29:40.445
That won't work.

00:29:40.528 --> 00:29:43.490
You can't get into Noah's Ark
with just a plate alone.

00:29:44.073 --> 00:29:47.160
You will need something to amplify
the magnetic field.

00:29:47.243 --> 00:29:49.579
I should've known you'd worked that out.

00:29:49.662 --> 00:29:52.415
You really are a clever one,
Professor Meyzel.

00:29:52.499 --> 00:29:55.418
But that isn't gonna be necessary.

00:29:55.502 --> 00:29:57.670
At least, not for me.

00:30:02.759 --> 00:30:06.221
Now, shall we carry on?

00:30:11.601 --> 00:30:13.186
-Yo, Jean!
-Huh?

00:30:13.269 --> 00:30:14.687
You all done now?

00:30:14.771 --> 00:30:15.980
You bonehead!

00:30:16.064 --> 00:30:18.525
It's entirely your fault
this happened again.

00:30:18.608 --> 00:30:23.363
I hate doing that.
There's just no elegance, whatsoever.

00:30:23.446 --> 00:30:26.533
Thanks a lot, Jean.

00:30:28.368 --> 00:30:31.287
And how did you get all beaten up
this time?

00:30:31.871 --> 00:30:33.581
He took the professor
and Margaret with him.

00:30:33.665 --> 00:30:37.418
Huh? He did what?
How could you just act like there's…

00:30:37.502 --> 00:30:39.420
Dammit!

00:30:42.507 --> 00:30:43.758
This is it!

00:30:44.342 --> 00:30:48.012
This is Noah's Ark!
Just as the ancient writings said!

00:30:48.096 --> 00:30:49.681
Ancient writings?

00:30:49.764 --> 00:30:52.934
At another site,
the Pentagon excavated a stone tablet

00:30:53.017 --> 00:30:54.602
that had been washed ashore.

00:30:54.686 --> 00:30:58.940
And written on that tablet
was the way to operate the Ark.

00:30:59.649 --> 00:31:03.695
However, much of what it said
was inconsistent with the Old Testament,

00:31:03.778 --> 00:31:05.113
so no one believed it.

00:31:05.613 --> 00:31:09.868
They didn't until ARCAM managed
to unearth this.

00:31:12.495 --> 00:31:14.581
That's ancient Hebrew writing.

00:31:14.664 --> 00:31:17.000
"I am God in Heaven above.

00:31:17.083 --> 00:31:19.794
You who awaken me,
the cincture of the earth,

00:31:19.878 --> 00:31:23.381
shall then bend to your every will.

00:31:24.132 --> 00:31:27.218
And thus, should evil break loose
upon the earth,

00:31:28.011 --> 00:31:30.471
take the grace of Heaven,
and make of it the Devil's fire."

00:31:31.806 --> 00:31:37.604
Yes, with this, one can alter the very
cincture of the earth, its atmosphere,

00:31:38.354 --> 00:31:41.608
and thus, manipulate the composition
of solar radiation.

00:31:42.567 --> 00:31:43.818
Meaning…

00:31:45.570 --> 00:31:49.198
Noah's Ark is a terraforming device.

00:31:52.076 --> 00:31:54.829
Is that kid trying to activate the Ark?

00:31:55.830 --> 00:31:59.584
Can you name the most
dire crisis faced by the modern world?

00:31:59.667 --> 00:32:02.045
Environmental destruction.

00:32:03.254 --> 00:32:09.218
Global warming, freak weather events,
water pollution, soil contamination,

00:32:09.302 --> 00:32:12.722
deforestation, desertification.

00:32:12.805 --> 00:32:16.017
However, once I possess Noah's Ark,

00:32:16.100 --> 00:32:18.853
all these problems
can be solved right now.

00:32:18.937 --> 00:32:21.397
Where the nuclear bomb symbolized power,

00:32:21.481 --> 00:32:24.859
Noah's Ark shall be a symbol of peace
and new beginnings.

00:32:25.443 --> 00:32:29.322
Utterly foolish.
Malicious posturing, that's all.

00:32:29.405 --> 00:32:32.325
America wanted the Ark
so they can show off.

00:32:33.034 --> 00:32:35.745
You're right, it is utterly foolish.

00:32:35.828 --> 00:32:36.746
Huh?

00:32:37.330 --> 00:32:40.583
And yet, I have to thank the Pentagon…

00:32:42.001 --> 00:32:47.006
for allowing me the opportunity
to pass judgment on humanity myself.

00:32:51.552 --> 00:32:53.179
Gravitational control.

00:33:04.983 --> 00:33:06.526
Jean!

00:33:06.609 --> 00:33:07.860
What?

00:33:10.071 --> 00:33:11.531
What the hell is this?

00:33:11.614 --> 00:33:13.241
It's full of dinosaurs.

00:33:13.324 --> 00:33:16.995
Not just dinosaurs,
creatures I've never seen before.

00:33:17.620 --> 00:33:20.456
You must've seen them
on the way here, Professor.

00:33:20.957 --> 00:33:24.752
All the creatures, most likely
subject of experiments

00:33:24.836 --> 00:33:27.672
to create the next generation of life.

00:33:27.755 --> 00:33:32.885
And in fact, that perfectly describes
the Ark's other magnificent power.

00:33:33.594 --> 00:33:36.139
Grace and destruction in equal measure?

00:33:36.222 --> 00:33:37.598
Exactly!

00:33:37.682 --> 00:33:40.768
The destruction wrought
by climate change in one hand.

00:33:40.852 --> 00:33:43.396
And the grace to recreate
life on earth in the other.

00:33:43.479 --> 00:33:46.315
You see, the second coming of Genesis

00:33:46.399 --> 00:33:49.569
is what Noah's Ark
was originally created for after all.

00:33:50.069 --> 00:33:51.612
It can't be…

00:33:52.321 --> 00:33:55.116
How about it, Professor Meyzel?

00:33:55.199 --> 00:33:56.868
Will you use the power of the Ark

00:33:56.951 --> 00:33:59.662
and help me create
the next generation of life?

00:33:59.746 --> 00:34:01.372
What are you talking about?

00:34:01.456 --> 00:34:04.042
Even if we fixed the earth's problem,

00:34:04.125 --> 00:34:07.670
humanity would just repeat
all the same mistakes.

00:34:07.754 --> 00:34:11.382
But with the Ark,
I will cleanse the world of humanity.

00:34:11.466 --> 00:34:13.801
And with the two of you by my side,

00:34:13.885 --> 00:34:15.470
I know that we can do it.

00:34:15.553 --> 00:34:18.681
Let us build a whole new world together.

00:34:22.935 --> 00:34:25.480
I won't do it.

00:34:27.315 --> 00:34:29.609
What did you say?

00:34:30.234 --> 00:34:31.944
I said I won't do it!

00:34:32.445 --> 00:34:34.906
I have no interest in helping you.

00:34:37.283 --> 00:34:41.370
Well, that's a shame.
I thought that you would understand.

00:34:43.790 --> 00:34:45.124
Margaret!

00:34:45.708 --> 00:34:47.752
The next time, I will kill her.

00:34:48.711 --> 00:34:51.422
You insolent foolish child.

00:34:55.301 --> 00:34:58.346
Hand over Margaret
and the professor. Do it!

00:34:59.806 --> 00:35:02.975
Wow. I didn't expect you back so soon.

00:35:03.059 --> 00:35:05.978
Please. I wasn't gonna die
without taking you with me.

00:35:06.062 --> 00:35:07.355
Oh, yeah?

00:35:07.438 --> 00:35:10.191
Do you really believe you can stop me?

00:35:11.109 --> 00:35:12.527
'Cause if you think you can,

00:35:13.277 --> 00:35:15.321
you are welcome to try.

00:35:31.504 --> 00:35:33.131
Hey, look!

00:35:37.051 --> 00:35:38.261
But that's…

00:35:40.471 --> 00:35:42.473
What have you done this time?

00:35:43.057 --> 00:35:46.853
Now I will use Noah's power
to raise the earth's temperature.

00:35:48.646 --> 00:35:51.524
And then the second Great Flood
shall begin.

00:35:54.610 --> 00:35:57.071
We're detecting changes
in the composition of the atmosphere,

00:35:57.155 --> 00:35:58.364
centered on Mount Ararat!

00:35:58.447 --> 00:36:01.033
We believe Noah's Ark
has been activated.

00:36:03.077 --> 00:36:06.372
Jean, take Margaret
and the professor and get out of here.

00:36:07.123 --> 00:36:10.543
You're so soft you couldn't bring yourself
to kill that wretch back there.

00:36:10.626 --> 00:36:13.629
I'm definitely not leaving you alone
with something like this.

00:36:14.380 --> 00:36:16.966
Margaret needs immediate
medical attention.

00:36:17.049 --> 00:36:19.635
With your speed,
you should make it in time.

00:36:20.678 --> 00:36:23.347
If you lose, I'll kill you.

00:36:23.431 --> 00:36:24.932
You're not leaving.

00:36:25.474 --> 00:36:27.101
Oh, no, you don't.

00:36:28.311 --> 00:36:31.314
A smokescreen?

00:36:31.397 --> 00:36:32.982
No!

00:36:37.445 --> 00:36:41.866
Hey, Colonel, the professor and Margaret
will leave unharmed.

00:36:41.949 --> 00:36:44.827
The one you need to worry about is me!

00:36:59.342 --> 00:37:00.676
Whoa!

00:37:02.845 --> 00:37:05.765
You still don't see, do you?

00:37:05.848 --> 00:37:09.268
You're proud of that outfit,
but it's not gonna stop me.

00:37:12.188 --> 00:37:14.232
And now, I must ask you to please leave.

00:37:14.815 --> 00:37:19.237
You're bleeding in God's chamber
and it so pains me to see it dirtied.

00:37:20.571 --> 00:37:22.782
God's chamber?

00:37:22.865 --> 00:37:27.328
Where the hell is God
supposed to be in here?

00:37:28.371 --> 00:37:29.830
Isn't it obvious?

00:37:29.914 --> 00:37:33.501
Noah, and I,
with the Ark's power, are Gods.

00:37:34.794 --> 00:37:37.797
And yet, you turn the Ark
into a genocide device?

00:37:39.048 --> 00:37:41.968
You really don't see
the bigger picture, do you?

00:37:42.551 --> 00:37:45.221
You see,
even if I hadn't triggered the Ark,

00:37:45.304 --> 00:37:47.807
sooner or later, humanity
would've destroyed the earth

00:37:47.890 --> 00:37:49.767
all by themselves anyway.

00:37:50.351 --> 00:37:53.562
It would've been way beyond the point
of any possible recovery.

00:37:54.563 --> 00:37:57.441
I'm sure you want to be
the hero who saves the world.

00:37:57.525 --> 00:38:00.987
But that is mere self-serving hypocrisy.

00:38:01.070 --> 00:38:02.655
You make me sick.

00:38:02.738 --> 00:38:04.573
Huh?

00:38:04.657 --> 00:38:05.992
Moron.

00:38:06.993 --> 00:38:11.038
Like I give a damn
about the end of humanity.

00:38:11.580 --> 00:38:14.000
Then why are you trying to stop me?

00:38:14.917 --> 00:38:17.003
The world is messed up,

00:38:17.795 --> 00:38:22.300
but everything important to me,
my friends and allies,

00:38:22.383 --> 00:38:24.010
they're all here.

00:38:24.093 --> 00:38:26.679
Friends, you say? And allies?

00:38:26.762 --> 00:38:29.765
Such things do not exist in this era.

00:38:31.350 --> 00:38:33.311
That just means that nobody likes you,

00:38:33.394 --> 00:38:35.771
so you wouldn't understand.

00:38:35.855 --> 00:38:37.398
Silence, you hypocrite!

00:38:45.489 --> 00:38:48.075
Oh no, I used too much power.

00:38:49.952 --> 00:38:53.748
This isn't over yet.

00:38:53.831 --> 00:38:55.708
I said silence!

00:38:55.791 --> 00:38:57.418
I am God!

00:38:57.501 --> 00:39:00.254
If I don't exterminate humanity
and their mistakes now,

00:39:00.338 --> 00:39:03.049
soon it'll be too late!

00:39:07.803 --> 00:39:09.847
Don't make me laugh.

00:39:11.057 --> 00:39:15.770
No God was made by humans.
You're just a fraud.

00:39:15.853 --> 00:39:16.896
Silen--

00:39:22.693 --> 00:39:26.113
If you ask me, you're the hypocrite.

00:39:26.197 --> 00:39:27.448
What?

00:39:27.948 --> 00:39:30.910
You say you wanna change the world,

00:39:30.993 --> 00:39:33.704
and you justify it by invoking God.

00:39:33.788 --> 00:39:35.122
No!

00:39:39.335 --> 00:39:42.088
But you do actually know, don't you?

00:39:42.713 --> 00:39:48.135
God is just an excuse people use
to run away from their sins.

00:39:48.219 --> 00:39:49.136
No!

00:39:49.887 --> 00:39:52.098
You are no God. You're…

00:39:52.932 --> 00:39:54.058
…human!

00:39:54.141 --> 00:39:55.017
No!

00:39:55.684 --> 00:39:58.020
Which means that the future of humanity

00:39:58.104 --> 00:40:00.731
will always be decided by us humans.

00:40:00.815 --> 00:40:02.066
No!

00:40:14.203 --> 00:40:15.830
The Ark has…

00:40:16.664 --> 00:40:18.207
stopped?

00:40:25.214 --> 00:40:26.424
Hey.

00:40:27.049 --> 00:40:28.968
So why didn't you finish me off?

00:40:29.844 --> 00:40:31.512
Don't get any ideas.

00:40:32.138 --> 00:40:35.307
Your words did not sway me.
The time has finally come.

00:40:36.517 --> 00:40:42.148
Just a little more, one step
further, and all the bad dreams…

00:40:43.023 --> 00:40:44.859
would've been washed away.

00:40:46.861 --> 00:40:49.280
Your dream playtime is over.

00:40:49.989 --> 00:40:51.198
We're going home.

00:40:51.282 --> 00:40:52.992
What are you doing?

00:40:53.075 --> 00:40:55.453
You think I'd just leave you here
still alive?

00:41:03.335 --> 00:41:04.712
What did you do?

00:41:05.629 --> 00:41:08.424
I activated the Ark's self-destruct mode.

00:41:09.633 --> 00:41:12.303
So now, time will return to the Ark

00:41:12.386 --> 00:41:15.473
and it'll be unable to sustain
the form it's in.

00:41:15.556 --> 00:41:20.895
With this, Noah and myself
shall disappear from this world forever.

00:41:20.978 --> 00:41:22.271
Damn twerp!

00:41:25.399 --> 00:41:30.279
I… was created for Noah.

00:41:31.906 --> 00:41:36.994
If the Ark is gone,
then I have no reason to exist.

00:41:39.413 --> 00:41:42.750
Goodbye, Yu Ominae.

00:41:43.792 --> 00:41:46.504
Charge ahead through
this screwed up world.

00:41:46.587 --> 00:41:51.091
Go fight it with all of your strength!

00:42:06.106 --> 00:42:07.399
Professor…

00:42:08.108 --> 00:42:11.737
Time was frozen for it,
but now it moves once more.

00:42:12.780 --> 00:42:14.573
That much mass,

00:42:14.657 --> 00:42:18.244
I doubt it can maintain its form
in three-dimensional space.

00:42:19.245 --> 00:42:23.624
Now, we can only watch it
as it crumbles to dust.

00:42:30.256 --> 00:42:31.840
Ominae.

00:42:32.591 --> 00:42:33.842
Wake up, Ominae!

00:42:35.261 --> 00:42:36.387
Honestly.

00:42:36.470 --> 00:42:39.807
If it weren't for me, that's now
a hundred times you'd have died.

00:42:43.185 --> 00:42:44.311
Jean.

00:42:44.395 --> 00:42:45.604
What?

00:42:45.688 --> 00:42:49.608
You were right. I am soft.

00:42:50.276 --> 00:42:53.737
I can still see the kid's face at the end.

00:42:54.321 --> 00:42:57.575
Yeah, you're
a bleeding-heart softie, for sure.

00:42:58.576 --> 00:43:02.663
But to be honest, that's something
I actually like about you.

00:43:02.746 --> 00:43:04.707
Hey, I heard that.

00:43:04.790 --> 00:43:07.001
No, you didn't. Now shut it and hold on.

00:43:14.091 --> 00:43:15.384
Seriously?

00:43:36.363 --> 00:43:37.531
It's over.

00:43:38.324 --> 00:43:41.452
Noah's Ark, it's all gone.

00:44:04.767 --> 00:44:07.186
Oh, this kid. He did it again.

00:44:07.269 --> 00:44:09.688
-We were so worried…
-We're fine. We're all okay now.

00:44:13.734 --> 00:44:14.943
You cocky punk.

00:44:15.027 --> 00:44:16.236
<i>Shut up.</i>

00:45:41.780 --> 00:45:43.615
Subtitle translation by: Zensho Yamamoto
